# RoadwiseFleet deploy notifier environment — KEY NAMES ONLY.
#
# Host path: /etc/roadwisefleet/notify.env   (mode 0600, root:root)
# Install:   sudo install -d -m 0755 /etc/roadwisefleet
#            sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root notify.env.example \
#              /etc/roadwisefleet/notify.env    # then fill in the values
#
# Used by /usr/local/bin/roadwise-notify.sh to post the "READY TO TEST" signal,
# the production promotion notice, and the deploy-failure alerts. Same
# secret-storage pattern as the rest of the pilot: a 0600 EnvironmentFile, no
# credential in a unit, a repo file, a command line, or a log.
#
# Configure ONE transport. Matrix is the one that works from elilavps2, where the
# deployer runs (elilavps2 cannot reach the relay — see transport 2).
#
# 1) Matrix bot -> the room that receives deploy signals (#eila). REQUIRED for
#    the deploy path to be able to signal at all; with no transport configured
#    roadwise-notify.sh exits 3 and the deployer records notify=not-sent-* in
#    deploy-state.json instead of pretending the owner was told.
#    Use a dedicated bot account; a token that can only send to that room is best.
# RWF_MATRIX_HOMESERVER=https://matrix.elilaltd.com
# RWF_MATRIX_ROOM_ID=!<roomid>:elilaltd.com
# RWF_MATRIX_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#
# 2) Orchestrator alert relay -> #eila-alerts. ADVANCED / usually WRONG here:
#    the relay is bound to 127.0.0.1:9099 on elilavps1 (loopback), so elilavps2
#    cannot reach it as deployed. Only set this if the URL really is reachable
#    from the host running the notifier, and only with a registered endpoint
#    (/alert, /gatus, /grafana) — the relay reads the JSON key "message".
#    Anything else (e.g. /notify) is refused, and an unreachable relay is a loud
#    failure (exit 4), never a silent skip.
# RWF_RELAY_URL=http://<reachable-host>:9099/alert
